From e787a605dcdb03200057b41ab73ea9941a7c89c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristian <kristian@apache.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:24:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Write Confluent protobuf rows with the schema of the
 table

The table handle carries the registry schema id and message the table
columns were derived from, and the page sink passes it to the encoder,
but the Confluent protobuf encoder ignored it and looked up the latest
schema of the subject again. A schema registered between describing
the table and writing it made INSERT encode the table's columns with a
schema they were not derived from: a column the new version renamed or
dropped failed the write, and the message of the subject could differ.

Encode with the schema id and message the data schema names, and keep
the latest schema only for a table that does not name one.
