From ebb1e71911151fc584017724aaa3bba44e603e60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristian <kristian@apache.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:24:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Take Kafka table columns from the table handle

getTableHandle looked up the table description once for the data
schemas and again for the columns, and getColumnHandles and the table
schema used in analysis looked it up a third and fourth time. A schema
registry based supplier resolves each lookup from the latest schema
versions, so a schema registered in between gave a query columns that
were not derived from the data schema it reads and writes with.

Build the handle's data schemas and columns from one description, and
answer getColumnHandles and getTableSchema from the handle.
