Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Check reserved protobuf declarations with the parser's
 matcher

The check for fields and enum values that reuse a reserved number or
name rebuilt the reserved ranges from the parser's Kotlin range values,
which made the record decoder declare the Kotlin standard library. The
parser's Reserved type already matches numbers and names, including
negative enum ranges, so use it and drop the dependency.
